+2.  **Virtual Pose Generation:** For each blurred image $k$, define the start pose $T_{start}^{(k)}$ and end pose $T_{end}^{(k)}$ [S1]. Generate $n$ virtual poses $T_i^{(k)}$ for $i=0 \dots n-1$ by interpolating between $T_{start}^{(k)}$ and $T_{end}^{(k)}$ [S1]. The interpolation method can be linear or cubic B-spline [S1].
+3.  **Virtual Image Synthesis:** For each virtual pose $T_i^{(k)}$, render a sharp virtual image $C_i^{(k)}(u)$ using standard 3D Gaussian Splatting rasterization [S1]. The pixel value at location $u$ is computed by sorting Gaussians front-to-back and compositing their contributions [S1]. The opacity contribution of a Gaussian $i$ is given by:
